tead of re-deriving or re-asking it.",    ["description.057"] = "Ask the user one question and wait for their answer. Use when a request is genuinely ambiguous -- two ways to read it, a choice of targets, a preference you cannot infer -- and answering it wrong would waste work. Offer concrete options when the plausible answers are few; omit them for an open question. The answer comes back as this call's result. You cannot ask from a subagent.",    ["description.058"] = "The question itself, one or two sentences, in the words you would use to the user.",    ["description.059"] = "The concrete answers to pick from, 2 to 4. Omit entirely for an open question.",    ["description.060"] = "Save a durable fact about this user or project under a short key. Survives context compaction and restarts. Use for preferences, paths and goals, not for transcript chatter.",    ["description.061"] = "List everything currently remembered, or read one key.",    ["description.062"] = "Delete one remembered key.",    ["description.063"] = "The complete task, including what counts as a finished answer.",    ["description.064"] = "Which tools it gets. 'read' cannot change anything; 'full' can. Unset uses the configured default, which is 'full'.",    ["description.065"] = "Send another message to a subagent that has already reported, keeping everything it found. Use this instead of dispatching a fresh one whenever you want more from the same investigation: 'you stopped at the step limit, carry on', 'now check X as well', 'quote that line verbatim'. It is far cheaper than a new dispatch, which would have to rediscover what this one already knows. Takes the id from the report. Blocks until it answers again.",    ["description.066"] = "The subagent's id, as printed in its report.",    ["description.067"] = "What you want from it now. It still cannot ask questions, so be complete.",    ["description.068"] = "Step limit for this follow-up, 1-30. Defaults to the configured one.",    ["description.069"] = "Pause for a few seconds before continuing, to let something in the game settle or a change take effect.",    ["description.070"] = "Read your character: position, health, movement values and what it is standing on.",    ["description.071"] = "Change movement or health values on your own character. Values a server owns will snap back.",    ["description.072"] = "Walk your character to a position using normal pathing, waiting until it arrives or gives up. Use this rather than teleporting when the server watches movement.",    ["description.073"] = "Move your character straight to a position. Client-side only, so a server with position checks may revert it.",    ["description.074"] = "Send a message into Roblox chat. Reports a failure if no channel is available.",    ["description.075"] = "Read a contiguous slice of a workspace file or saved paste. The result includes a continuation offset when more remains.",    ["description.076"] = "Replace exact text in a workspace file without rewriting the whole file. Read it first. Refuses missing or ambiguous matches unless replace_all is true, and refuses an edit if the file changed while it was being prepared. Files and edited output are limited to 2 MB.",    ["description.077"] = "Create a workspace file or replace most of its content (up to 2 MiB per call). Parent folders are created. ",    ["description.078"] = "Append up to 2 MiB to a workspace file, creating it if needed. Prefer small additions.",    ["description.079"] = "Delete a file or folder from your workspace. This cannot be undone.",    ["description.080"] = "Find literal text across workspace files or saved pastes in one call. Returns matching lines, byte offsets and a continuation cursor. Searches subfolders; skips binary/files over 2 MB. Bounds directory, file and byte scans.",    ["description.081"] = "Read up to 12 workspace files or saved pastes in one call, sharing the result budget. Each slice includes continuation offsets. Individual failures preserve other results.",    ["description.082"] = "Apply up to 20 exact edits to one workspace file in one write. Edits are evaluated in order. All must validate before writing; refuses stale contents. Empty new_text deletes. File/output limit 2 MB.",    ["description.083"] = "Download and run the official Project Gravity loader in this client, then report the live status. Use this when gravity_status shows Gravity is not loaded. If Gravity is already connected this reports that without reloading; pass force=true to re-run the loader, which reloads Gravity and releases held parts. This fetches and executes remote code from the Project Gravity repository.",    ["description.084"] = "List the live Gravity shape catalog, or pass name to inspect a shape's real control keys, values, buttons and stored-unit slider ranges. No hardcoded catalog.",    ["description.085"] = "Control Gravity using native handlers: start/recenter (defaults to your character), stop and release parts, pause/resume, enable/disable, reroll, reset_settings (all engine/shape settings and keybinds to defaults), or launch/charge a manually controlled Slingshot.",    ["description.086"] = "Change Gravity engine, formation, interface, performance and Part Control panel defaults using native names. Validates the whole batch, applies native effects, refreshes controls and requests a save. PartCtl* are panel defaults; use gravity_part_control to change selected parts. Read gravity_status first.",    ["description.087"] = "Select a Gravity shape, configure its control keys, or press one real Button. Inspect gravity_shapes(name=...) first. Values use stored units (display divided by Div). Buttons require that shape to be selected and never become settings.",    ["description.088"] = "Set Gravity's anchor to yourself or all players, add/remove a specific target, or clear targeting. Ambiguous player names are refused. Preserves the native Targets table.",    ["description.089"] = "Set or clear one native Gravity